Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC34; groundwork for AC30, AC47, AC48)
Research: Q12 (upstream_aborted)
Why this approach: the watchers hang off Meta (watchRequestBody / watchResponseBody, requestBodyErr / responseBodyErr, all unexported) so the proxy and Settle share one place; the request side keeps its first error with atomic.Pointer CompareAndSwap because the transport reads it on its own goroutine, the response side is a plain field because it is read on the handler's goroutine. Tests in core_test reach them through export_test.go.
Alternatives rejected: exporting the watchers (they are an implementation detail of the proxy); one shared watcher type with an atomic on both sides (the response side does not need it).
Trade-off / known limit: Meta's unexported start time is not added yet; it lands with the proxy (T8+) where it is first used, since an unused field fails lint. Settle is nil-safe so a defer on a missing Meta does nothing.
